{%- comment -%}
  Sample scans, click to open full screen.

  Split out of tonescan-landing so the page composes from real sections in a JSON
  template. Page-wide CSS and JS are rendered once by layout/tonescan.liquid, so this
  file carries markup only and can be reordered or removed without taking them with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="tonescan-landing tw:text-neutral-200">
  {%- comment -%} Screenshots live in Shopify Files (Content > Files). {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ts_cdn = 'https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0634/3199/9736/files' -%}

  <section id="gallery" class="ts-clip-x tw:mx-auto tw:w-full tw:max-w-[1400px] tw:scroll-mt-[84px] tw:px-[15px] tw:py-[80px] tw:md:px-[50px] tw:md:py-[120px]">
    <div class="tw:mx-auto tw:max-w-[720px] tw:text-center">
      <p class="tw:mb-[16px] tw:text-[13px] tw:font-semibold tw:uppercase tw:tracking-[0.16em] tw:text-[#60a5fa]">Sample scans</p>
      <h2 class="tw:text-[32px] tw:font-semibold tw:leading-[1.1] tw:tracking-[-0.02em] tw:text-white tw:md:text-[46px]">Real scans, real detail.</h2>
      <p class="tw:mx-auto tw:mt-[16px] tw:max-w-[560px] tw:text-[16px] tw:text-neutral-400">Every frame below was converted with toneScan Studio. Click any one to see it full-screen.</p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      ⚠️ BEFORE LAUNCH, TWO THINGS.
      1. ADD MORE FRAMES. ts_scan_list below is the single source for the marquee: one URL per
         line, any number. There are only FIVE real converted frames available right now, so
         across 30 tiles each one repeats about six times, visibly. Aim for ~30 unique frames.
      2. FILL IN THE CAPTURE DETAILS. The data-camera / data-lens / data-light / data-film /
         data-shot / data-format values are intentionally EMPTY: the originals were invented
         placeholders and this page is public, so nothing unverified ships. Empty renders as a
         hidden row, and the whole metadata panel stays hidden until at least one is filled.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      One line per frame: URL,width,height, PhotoSwipe needs the real pixel size up front to
      size the zoomed view, so the dimensions have to travel with the URL.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture ts_scan_data -%}
{{ ts_cdn }}/DSCF0079_RGB-pos.jpg,2400,1626;{{ ts_cdn }}/DSCF0025_RGB-pos.jpg,2400,1626;{{ ts_cdn }}/DSCF0049_RGB-pos.jpg,2400,1626;{{ ts_cdn }}/DSCF0028_RGB-pos.jpg,2400,1626;{{ 'converted.jpg' | asset_url }},1500,1017
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign ts_scan_items = ts_scan_data | strip | split: ';' -%}
    {%- assign ts_rows = 2 -%}
    {%- assign ts_per_row = 12 -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Two rows running in opposite directions. Each track is rendered TWICE and shifted
      -50%, so the loop is seamless, that means the two passes must stay identical, and tile
      width has to come from margin-right rather than gap or the halves don't line up.
      Frames are dealt out round-robin so a short source list still varies row to row.
      data-scan-index points at the entry in the JSON below; duplicated tiles reuse it, so the
      viewer shows each frame once no matter how many times it appears on screen.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="ts-gallery tw:mt-[48px]">
      {%- for row in (1..ts_rows) -%}
        {%- assign row_i = row | minus: 1 -%}
        <div class="ts-mq {% cycle 'ts-mq--l', 'ts-mq--r' %}">
          <div class="ts-mq__track">
            {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
              {%- for n in (1..ts_per_row) -%}
                {%- assign slot = n | minus: 1 | times: ts_rows | plus: row_i -%}
                {%- assign pick = slot | modulo: ts_scan_items.size -%}
                {%- assign ts_parts = ts_scan_items[pick] | split: ',' -%}
                <a class="ts-scan" href="{{ ts_parts[0] }}" data-scan-index="{{ pick }}"
                   {% if pass == 2 %}aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"{% endif %}
                   aria-label="View this frame full-screen">
                  <span class="ts-scan__img" style="background-image:url('{{ ts_parts[0] }}')"></span>
                </a>
              {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} slide list for PhotoSwipe, one entry per unique frame {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="application/json" class="ts-gallery-data">
      [{% for it in ts_scan_items %}{% assign pp = it | split: ',' %}{% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{"src":{{ pp[0] | json }},"width":{{ pp[1] }},"height":{{ pp[2] }},"alt":"A film frame converted with toneScan Studio"}{% endfor %}]
    </script>
  </section>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "toneScan gallery",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "settings": [],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "toneScan gallery"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
